# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Skills are read, sliced, and digested as bytes: prompt sections are extracted
# from Markdown by heading, schemas are hashed, and reports are matched against
# exact markers. A CRLF checkout on Windows changes those bytes, so the same
# skill would produce different digests and different prompt text depending on
# the host it was cloned to. Normalizing at checkout keeps one skill one thing.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
